ions to  do things that are expensive now but  will benefit the future but you then  think about how politics actually works  and there's no incentive to do that that  if you are the president of the u.s  today  and you do something today that's  politically expensive and the result is  that america is better off 20 years from  now  20 years from now you're long out of  office 50 50 chances of  the president of the other party uh  and you're more likely to be out office  because you spent your political  resources doing that instead of doing  things that would get you votes  so if you actually look at how  politicians act they  base their decisions mainly on the  effect of the next election  which is sensible to do and so if you  have an issue like global warming for  example  they tell a good story about how we've  got a sacrifice now for the future  it's conceivable that they're right that  it does good i'm somewhat skeptical i  think people exaggerate the amount of  danger in global warming but i could be  wrong but the reason they're doing it  is not that they care about what happens  50 years from now when they're going to  be dead  it's they think they can get political  benefit by doing it now  after all if you have a carbon tax  that's a new source of revenue  government politicians always like to  have money to spend  and just like the rest of us uh so  uh if you're in a poor third world  country  you'd like to push the idea of global  warming in order to persuade the rich  countries to give you some money  so i think if you if you ask on any of  these issues  not what you not what could government  do that's good or what would you like  government to do  but what's the best theory you can offer  as to what government will do i think  that's  that's an attitude that is worth worth  promoting  for more debates talks and interviews  subscribe today  to the institute of art and ideas at iai  tv

